// An act whose domain is not enumerable is lawful when its `Holds when` is true of the instance asked about (D15, brief B11); no instance is materialised, and an assignment still beats the rule.
Fact member Identified by Ann, Ben
Function basis Identified by member * int
Act transfer Actor member Recipient member' Related to int
  Holds when (Exists basis: basis.member == member && basis.int >= int)
  Valid when member != member'
  Creates (Foreach basis: basis(member, basis.int - int) When basis.member == member)
        , (Foreach basis: basis(member', basis.int + int) When basis.member == member').
+basis(Ann, 5). +basis(Ben, 0).
?lawful transfer(Ann, Ben, 4).
?Enabled(transfer(Ann, Ben, 5)).
?transfer(Ann, Ben, 5).
?!lawful transfer(Ann, Ben, 7).
?!lawful transfer(Ben, Ann, 1).
transfer(Ann, Ben, 4).
?basis(Ann, 1). ?basis(Ben, 4).
?!lawful transfer(Ann, Ben, 2).
?lawful transfer(Ben, Ann, 3).
-transfer(Ben, Ann, 3).
?!lawful transfer(Ben, Ann, 3).
?lawful transfer(Ben, Ann, 2).
